{"name":"Lotus Flower","hex":"#f4f0da","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lotus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of the genus Nelumbo of aquatic plants in the family Nelumbonaceae.","A water lily (Nymphaea), especially those of Egypt or India. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lotus"},{"term":"flower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorful, conspicuous structure associated with angiosperms, frequently scented and attracting various insects, and which may or may not be used for sexual reproduction.","A reproductive structure in angiosperms (flowering plants), often conspicuously colourful and typically including sepals, petals, and either or both stamens and/or a pistil."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put forth blooms.","To decorate with pictures of flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flower"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lotus Flower (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lotus Flower\" is a song by the English rock band Radiohead, released as the lead single from their eighth studio album, The King of Limbs (2011). It features Thom Yorke's falsetto over syncopated beats and a synthesiser bassline. Its music video, featuring Yorke's erratic dancing, attracted millions of views and inspired an internet meme."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b2/Radiohead_-_Lotus_Flower_cover_art.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lotus_Flower_(song)","wikidata":"Q3296904"},{"title":"Lotus Flower (Woody Shaw album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lotus Flower is an album led by trumpeter Woody Shaw which was recorded in 1982 and released on the Enja label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e7/Lotus_Flower_%28Woody_Shaw_album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lotus_Flower_(Woody_Shaw_album)","wikidata":"Q17035557"},{"title":"Nelumbo nucifera","blocks":[{"text":"Nelumbo nucifera, also known as Padma or Kamala, sacred lotus, pink lotus, Indian lotus, or simply lotus, is one of two extant species of aquatic plant in the family Nelumbonaceae. It is sometimes colloquially called water lily, though this more often refers to members of the family Nymphaeaceae. The lotus belongs in the order Proteales."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg/330px-Sacred_lotus_Nelumbo_nucifera.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelumbo_nucifera","wikidata":"Q16528"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower","wikidata":"Q506"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2008-0419-GarthJennings.jpg/500px-2008-0419-GarthJennings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2008-0419-GarthJennings.jpg/500px-2008-0419-GarthJennings.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Garth Jennings directed the \"Lotus Flower\" music video.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2008-0419-GarthJennings.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lotus_field.jpg/120px-Lotus_field.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lotus_field.jpg/250px-Lotus_field.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lotus_field.jpg/120px-Lotus_field.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALotus_field.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Nelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg/250px-Nelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Nelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg/330px-Nelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Nelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg/250px-Nelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANelumbo_July_2011-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Nelumbo_nucifera_LOTUS_bud.jpg/250px-Nelumbo_nucifera_LOTUS_bud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Nelumbo_nucifera_LOTUS_bud.jpg/330px-Nelumbo_nucifera_LOTUS_bud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Nelumbo_nucifera_LOTUS_bud.jpg/250px-Nelumbo_nucifera_LOTUS_bud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","l